<title>UK: MAM squeezed higher amid stock shortage.</title>
<headline>MAM squeezed higher amid stock shortage.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mercury Asset Management Group Plc (MAM) shares were squeezed higher amid a shortage of stock on the view the stock has underperformed recently, dealers said.</p>
<p>MAM rose 65p to 13.45 stg by 0932 GMT.</p>
<p>&quot;There are a couple of buyers at the 13 quid (stg) level and an agency broker who is short,&quot; said one dealer.</p>
<p>MAM stood at 12.52 stg a share on Tuesday, July 22, and had underperformed the FTSE 100 by 18 percent since May 29.</p>
<p>-- Louise Ireland, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8712</p>
